## Context

Child of 0700. Closing the collection: the pool is frozen when all routes of the
protocol are executed or declared impossible, and the whole pool is screened.
This ticket carries the freeze deliverables.

Interim freeze possible before closing: the `icf_screen` table (1655) is
append-only; the screen of the existing stock stays valid, only additions are
screened. The diagram counts are fixed only at the final freeze.

Pieces already in draft (branch of ticket 1530): provisional structure and
figures of the diagram in `conception/rel-prisma-flux-provisoire.md`, annex
`conception/rel-sud-et-langues-annexe-brouillon.md`, Astra's review note.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Protocol updated and reconciled with the `origin/main` version: three-stage screen, sentinels fixed, two chaining rounds, non-OpenAlex sources, reserves, BRICS rule
- [ ] PRISMA diagram: counts rebuilt by script from the registries and the `icf_screen` table, identification by source and by date (PRISMA-S)
- [ ] Automation declared: models, versions, prompts, agreements measured with the reference judge
- [ ] Method paragraph written with the final counts
- [ ] Freeze manifest: file hashes, code SHA, DVC lock, model and prompt versions
- [ ] Reproduction package: configurations, code, registries and outputs of each pass, prompts (including stage 2), sentinels, advisor outputs
- [ ] Reserve sentinels reported apart from tuning ones
